iq-added-html-shadow-dom.answer:
- The Shadow DOM is an encapsulated subtree attached to a host, often in web components.
- The style scope isolates the internals
- slots project light-DOM content.
- It is different from React's render representation, and it is not a security boundary.
- Composed events/inherited CSS can cross the boundaries.
- The example uses fixed trusted markup
- do not interpolate an untrusted string into innerHTML.

```js
const host = document.createElement('div');
const shadow = host.attachShadow({mode: 'open'});
shadow.innerHTML = '<style>p { color: teal; }</style><p>Local styling</p>';
