- Fix the casing of console.log and call the function
- a definition alone prints nothing.
- In an ordinary run the logs 0–5 become eligible after the requested delay.
- Every let iteration has its own binding.
- With var, all the callbacks see the final value 6 of the shared function-scoped i.
- The delay is the earliest scheduling threshold, not an exact appointment time
- with i<5 the count/final value change.

```js
function sample() {
  for (let i = 0; i <= 5; i++) setTimeout(() => console.log(i), 1000);
}
sample();
