- Props are inputs from the parent
- state is changing data owned by the component, whose updates can schedule a render.
- A child must not update the parent by mutating a received object.
- children is the prop for nested content, useful for reusable shells.
- Panel owns the outer structure, the caller supplies the content.
- Children is not limited to one element or an array; it can be various React nodes.
- A distinct actions slot can give a clearer contract.

